/**
 * TASK: Accept a new task either from the Add button or from the Enter key.
 *
 * A JTextField fires an ActionEvent of its very own when the user presses
 * Enter in it, so ONE ActionListener can serve both the field named "entry"
 * and the button named "add".
 *
 * Complete actionPerformed so that every event:
 *   1. reads the field's text and trims it,
 *   2. does nothing at all when the trimmed text is empty,
 *   3. otherwise appends the trimmed text to the tasks list, clears the
 *      field back to "", and sets the label named "count" to
 *      "<n> task(s)".
 *
 * Example: type "milk" and press Enter -> tasks() is [milk], the field is
 * empty again and the label reads "1 task(s)".
 */
